        </p>
        <p>
          Our pro compiler handles Indic syllables algorithmically. It splits text into consonant clusters, isolates vowel matras, and arranges them in the precise pre-base and post-base layout required by Anu 7.0. It also filters archaic Telugu letters in the reverse direction to ensure you get clean, standard modern Telugu when converting legacy content back to Unicode.
        </p>
